# Copy to .env.local for local development. Never commit real values.
#
# On AWS:
# - SITE_ENV, SITE_URL and SECRETS_PATH are worked out from the branch name in amplify.yml. Nothing is set in
#   Amplify's environment variables.
# - Parameter Store, as SecureStrings: everything marked [secret]. The site reads them at runtime (src/lib/secrets.ts).
#   [shared secret] ones are the same on every branch and go once under /saigon-tailors, e.g. /saigon-tailors/SMTP_PASS.
#   [secret] ones differ per branch and go under SECRETS_PATH, e.g. /saigon-tailors/main/STRIPE_SECRET_KEY.

# Which build this is. Only main is "production"; anything else is hidden from search engines. Leave empty locally.
SITE_ENV=
# The site's public address, for Stripe's return links. Leave empty locally (http://localhost:3000 is used).
SITE_URL=

# This branch's folder for [secret] ones in Parameter Store (Sydney), e.g. /saigon-tailors/main.
# Leave empty locally and secrets come from this file, or set /saigon-tailors/development to read them from AWS.
SECRETS_PATH=

# Contact form email, sent from and to the Zoho mailbox in src/config.ts (needs a paid Zoho plan).
# [shared secret] An app-specific password for that mailbox (Account → Security → App Passwords), never the login password.
SMTP_PASS=

# Cloudflare Turnstile (dash.cloudflare.com → Turnstile). One widget for every branch: add each branch's hostname to
# it in Cloudflare. Its public site key is in src/config.ts. Development always uses
# Cloudflare's test keys, so leave this empty locally.
# [shared secret]
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# Booking and the travel fee. See docs/tech-stack.md.
# [shared secret] Cal.com → Settings → Developer → API keys.
CAL_API_KEY=
# [shared secret] A random string you make up and paste into the "Booking created" webhook's Secret field in Cal.com.
# Only main gets that webhook: one on development would settle real bookings in Stripe's test mode and cancel them.
# Leave empty locally (Cal.com can't reach your computer).
CAL_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# [secret] Stripe → Developers → API keys (sk_test_… until launch).
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# [secret] The signing secret of the webhook for checkout.session.expired.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
